#problem statement: To install tomcat server on Linux application server and deploy provided application. The deployed application should be accessible on port 6300 instead of default 8080 port.

1.  Login into application server 1 using ssh, and provide password once prompted.
            ssh username@hostname
2. Install tomcat on server using below mentioned command
            sudo yum install -y tomcat tomcat-webapps tomcat-admin-webapps
3. Enable and start tomcat service
            sudo systemctl enable tomcat
            sudo systemctl start tomcat
4. Check if tomcat service is started or failed using below command
            sudo systemctl status tomcat
5. If tomcat service is started then we are good to go for next steps
6. As per instructions we need to make sure application to be deployed is accessible at port 6300. Hence, we would need to update settings.xml available under /etc/tomcat/ Also, we need to locate Connector element for HTTP/1.1. Once we have that, change it to use 6300 as a port. Below is the example for the reference
            <Connector port="6300" protocol="HTTP/1.1"
            connectionTimeout="20000"
            redirectPort="8443" />                                                
7. Save the settings.xml
8. Next step is to copy/move artifact under /var/lib/tomcat/webapps/ directory.
9. Make sure you don't have same name of file or directory in /var/lib/tomcat/webapps/ directory and if present remove it using rm command.
10. Last step is to restart tomcat so that newly placed application will deployed
            sudo systemctl restart tomcat
11. Now our application is deployed on tomcat. To validate, use curl command from either jump server or another server in the domain.
            curl http://hostname_of_server_where_tomcat_is_installed:6300            